{"parentUuid":"071dc868-047f-4f21-84e0-4443078cfe95","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNK7L2B7PZw3724VZpXV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GjBttLLYB62mULR5AviiUu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-mcp-reach; S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad; gh pr view 477 --repo entireio/entire-brain --json body --jq .body > \"$S/pr477-body.md\"; python3 - \"$S/pr477-body.md\" <<'PY'\nimport sys\np=sys.argv[1]; s=open(p).read()\nadd = \"\"\"\n## Merged main, and the gap that exposed\n\nmain's COR-2268 refactor moved `resolveLocalTargetRepoDir` into\n`internal/cli/internal/base` on the very line this branch adds the check to\ndoctor. Resolving that is mechanical — keep both.\n\nRe-proving the resolution was not. Unwiring the check from doctor entirely left\n**every guard in this file green**: they all call `checkMCPSurfaceReachable`\ndirectly, so none of them could observe whether doctor runs it. That is the\nsame call-site blind spot that produced the fork bomb and the stderr race\nalready fixed on this branch — the logic lived in the *presence* of a call,\nwhich no test reached.\n\nDoctor now calls through a `doctorMCPSurfaceCheck` var, so\n`TestDoctorActuallyRunsTheMCPSurfaceCheck` proves the wiring against a real\nrepo fixture without spawning anything. Removing the call turns it red.\n\n\"\"\"\nmarker = \"🤖 Generated with\"\nassert s.count(marker)==1\ns = s.replace(marker, add.lstrip(\"\\n\") + marker)\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"body updated\")\nPY\ngh pr edit 477 --repo entireio/entire-brain --body-file \"$S/pr477-body.md\" && echo \"pushed\"","description":"Update 477's PR body"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":695,"cache_read_input_tokens":172351,"output_tokens"