{"parentUuid":"3c323e42-9028-4fad-9ab6-2ce20dd40bb6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9954bf2b-2065-478a-a1f3-5df6c17bcb36","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0141P9tqWzoD6pyK2fMTCcot","type":"tool_result","content":"List findings for a trail\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail finding list [<trail>] [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --cursor string       Continue from the next cursor returned by a previous page\n      --freshness string    Filter code-version freshness: current,stale,any (default \"current\")\n  -h, --help                help for list\n      --include-dismissed   Include dismissed findings\n      --json                Output as JSON\n  -n, --limit int           Maximum number of findings to show (default 100)\n      --severity string     Filter by comma-separated severity value(s): high,medium,low\n      --status string       Filter by lifecycle status(es): open,resolved,dismissed; use 'any' for all (default \"open\")\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --branch string    Select a repository branch within the trail\n      --context name     Act as this saved login name for this command only — including the git and agent processes it spawns — instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --project string   Project as gh/<owner> or et/<project>; required for list, otherwise defaults to the repository's namespace\n      --repo string      Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; for list, only filters the required --project\n      --trail string     Project trail number, ID, or <repo>/<number> (defaults to the current branch's parent)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cd015f94-1427-462c-b777-3241e0ab8b89","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:21:19.512Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"List findings for a trail\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail finding list [<trail>] [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --cursor string       Continue from the next cursor returned by a previous page\n      --freshness string    Filter code-version 