{"parentUuid":"619b1b0a-2b56-466a-ab52-23bb453b75d1","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_012T4LQvaPk5UVznnFZLm73a","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"M=/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory; rtk ls \\\"$M\\\" | grep -iE \\\"callsite|call-site|logic-in|trail-finding\\\"; echo \\\"--- logic-in-the-call-site ---\\\"; rtk read \\\"$M/logic-in-the-call-site.md\\\" 2>/dev/null | head -30\",\"description\":\"Check existing memory files\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":13},"type":"attachment","uuid":"71986fa0-79c2-4318-8cd5-685c612d47f9","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:24:13.977Z","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-firstrun-gate","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"619b1b0a-2b56-466a-ab52-23bb453b75d1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9954bf2b-2065-478a-a1f3-5df6c17bcb36","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012T4LQvaPk5UVznnFZLm73a","type":"tool_result","content":"logic-in-the-call-site.md  2.2K\ntrail-finding-sweep-pitfalls.md  3.0K\n--- logic-in-the-call-site ---\n---\nname: logic-in-the-call-site\ndescription: \"Defects that live in the ORDER of two calls, not in either function — no suite can reach them; extract the decision into a value\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5\n  modified: 2026-09-27T20:59:48.068Z\n---\n\nFive defects in one session on entire-graph's `bench/locate` lived in a **call site**, not in any\nfunction. Every one was invisible to a green suite, because a test can call a function and check\nits return; it cannot see that the caller invoked it too late.\n\n- receipts were written **after** the admission gate, so a dropped case left no argv, exit code\n  or raw bytes — the attempt most worth inspecting recorded nothing\n- the oracle was tallied **after** the gate, silently redefining its denominator as \"valid oracle\n  runs among paired-admitted cases\"; an audit found 20 valid receipts against a manifest saying 19\n- the seal was written by a *separate preflight*, so nothing bound directory, queries, run and\n  manifest together\n- the manifest's seal binding was a literal in the main block\n- `--diagnostic-dirty-build` was stripped from argv while a second flag was not, so the second\n  was parsed as a positional\n\n**Why:** the mutation sweep reports these as \"guard not held\" and the instinct is to write another\nassertion about the function — which passes, and changes nothing.\n\n**How to apply:** when a fix is \"call X before Y\", make the decision a **value a test can read** —\n`record_attempt` returning admission, `tally_oracle` taking state, `new_manifest(seal_sha, …)`.\nWhere the loop itself can't be imported (it lives in `__main__`), assert the ordering from","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"654d6a6b-3966-4a85-873f-8e14073ba410","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:24:16.526Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"logic-in-the-call-site.md  2.2K\ntrail-finding-sweep-pitfalls.md  3.0K\n--- logic-in-the-call-site ---\n---\nname: logic-in-the-call-site\ndescription: \"Defects that live in the ORDER of two calls, not in either function — no suite can reach them; extract the decision into a value\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5\n  modified: 2026-09-27T20:59:48.068Z\n---\n\nFive defects in one session on entire-graph's `bench/locate` lived in a **call site**, not in any\nfunction. Every one was invisible to a green suite, because a test can call a function and check\nits return; it cannot see that the caller invoked it too late.\n\n- receipts were written **after** the admission gate, so a dropped case left no argv, exit code\n  or raw bytes — the attempt most worth inspecting recorded nothing\n- the oracle was tallied **after** the gate, silently redefining its denominator as \"valid oracle\n  runs among paired-admitted cases\"; an audit found 20 valid receipts against a manifest saying 19\n- the seal was written by a *separate preflight*, so nothing bound directory, queries, run and\n  manifest together\n- the manifest's seal binding was a literal in the main block\n- `--diagnostic-dirty-build` was stripped from argv while a second flag was not, so the second\n  was parsed as a positional\n\n**Why:** the mutation sweep reports these as \"guard not held\" and the instinct is to write another\nassertion about the function — which passes, and changes nothing.\n\n**How to apply:** when a fix is \"call X before Y\", make the decision a **value a test can read** —\n`record_attempt` returning admission, `tally_oracle` taking state, `new_manifest(seal_sha, …)`.\nWhere the loop itself can't be imported (it lives in `__main__`), assert the ordering from","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"86a6a46a-b126-465a-b11d-701da0fdc4b9","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-firstrun-gate","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-firstrun-gate","branch":"fix/firstrun-agent-hook-paths","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"entireio","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entiredb","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entire.io","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-firstrun-gate","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"619b1b0a-2b56-466a-ab52-23bb453b75d1","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-firstrun-gate","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
