{"parentUuid":"32d1b507-7460-4822-8988-daf302659e28","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNKa8ZMZS6HV2URzUFEu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GFfSSB29oUUDEEDtxe5AXu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-firstrun-gate; for pair in \"477:388\" \"483:394\" \"484:395\" \"489:400\"; do n=${pair%%:*}; t=${pair#*:}; echo \"=========== PR#$n (trail $t) ===========\"; entire trail finding list --trail \"entire-brain/$t\" --status any --freshness any --json 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\nfor f in d.get('findings',[]):\n    print(f\\\"  [{f.get('status')}] sev={f.get('severity')} fresh={f.get('freshness','?')} id={f.get('id','?')[:12]}\\\")\n    print(f\\\"    title: {f.get('title','')}\\\")\n    loc=f.get('location') or {}\n    print(f\\\"    where: {loc.get('path','?')}:{loc.get('startLine','?')}\\\")\n    b=(f.get('body') or f.get('description') or '').replace(chr(10),' ')\n    print(f\\\"    body : {b[:400]}\\\")\n\"; done","description":"Read the open findings in detail"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1397,"cache_read_input_tokens":211071,"output_tokens":770,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":285},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1397,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":770,"cache_read_input_tokens":211071,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1397,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1397},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01GFfSSB29oUUDEEDtxe5AXu":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-firstrun-gate; for pair in \"477:388\" \"483:394\" \"484:395\" \"489:400\"; do n=${pair%%:*}; t=${pair#*:}; echo \"=========== PR#$n (trail $t) ===========\"; entire trail finding list --trail \"entire-brain/$t\" --status any --freshness any --json 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\nfor f in d.get('findings',[]):\n    print(f\\\"  [{f.get('status')}] sev={f.get('severity')} fresh={f.get('freshness','?')} id={f.get('id','?')[:12]}\\\")\n    print(f\\\"    title: {f.get('title','')}\\\")\n    loc=f.get('location') or {}\n    print(f\\\"    where: {loc.get('path','?')}:{loc.get('startLine','?')}\\\")\n    b=(f.get('body') or f.get('description') or '').replace(chr(10),' ')\n    print(f\\\"    body : {b[:400]}\\\")\n\"; done","description":"Read the open findings in detail"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"8b555f99-4719-4b3d-b0f5-fac6423567e7","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgNKa7rSLmM4gNcJQq932","requestRef":"573b2d40-de7c-4daf-9233-76b24b695969","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"d9c89d8a-a612-4bc8-b81e-3008446374b2","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:26:03.006Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-firstrun-gate","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"d9c89d8a-a612-4bc8-b81e-3008446374b2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9954bf2b-2065-478a-a1f3-5df6c17bcb36","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GFfSSB29oUUDEEDtxe5AXu","type":"tool_result","content":"=========== PR#477 (trail 388) ===========\n  [open] sev=low fresh=? id=01M5QWT2Y3Q1\n    title: None\n    where: ?:205\n    body : `readMCPFrame` allocates `make([]byte, length)` from the child's `Content-Length` with no upper bound. A misbehaving binary can make doctor try a multi-GB allocation before the timeout applies. Cap the length (for example a few MiB) and return an error beyond it.\n  [open] sev=low fresh=? id=01M5QM1M0BN3\n    title: None\n    where: ?:177\n    body : `readMCPFrame` allocates `make([]byte, length)` from the server-supplied `Content-Length` with no upper bound. A wrong or misbehaving binary can announce a huge length and cause a panic or out-of-memory error in doctor. Cap the length, which is the bounded-frames requirement at MCP boundaries.\n  [open] sev=medium fresh=? id=01M5QM1KZVGF\n    title: None\n    where: ?:219\n    body : With the opt-in set, `checkMCPSurfaceReachable` uses `os.Executable()`, which under `go test` is the test binary. The probe runs `<testbinary> mcp`, and the child re-runs the whole suite, including this test. That spawns another child, so the recursion is bounded only by the 20s probe timeouts. Inject the binary path, or stub the probe, in this test.\n=========== PR#483 (trail 394) ===========\n  [open] sev=medium fresh=? id=01M5R8FS7JTP\n    title: None\n    where: ?:1259\n    body : The oversize skip is applied to the identity capture, the full index build and `collectHistorySessionDigests`. The short-term delta path in `history_delta.go` also calls `readHistorySessionInventoryFile`, and `shortTermCanonicalInputRefusal` still treats `memory_input_too_large` as a refusal of the entire delta. A single oversize transcript therefore still blocks the overlay for every other sessio\n=========== PR#484 (trail 395) ===========\n  [open] sev=low fresh=? id=01M5RFGAVDQ2\n    title: None\n    where: ?:323\n    body : `graphContextAllowsAncestor` memoizes the probe result even when the probe failed (timeout, cancelled ctx, transient subprocess error). That permanently caches `false` for the binary for the life of the process, so a provider that supports `--allow-ancestor` is never asked for it again. Cache only successful probe results (a parsed report) and let failures retry.\n  [open] sev=medium fresh=? id=01M5R9TCX0J1\n    title: None\n    where: ?:264\n    body : `Unreliable` is built only from changed files that the answer returned records for. The `graphContextStale` contract says an ancestor store has already dropped the records for changed files, so those paths will mostly be absent from `symbols` and `tests`. `Unreliable` will then usually be empty even when the answer is incomplete, and a reader could take that as 'nothing unreliable'. The paths the \n=========== PR#489 (trail 400) ===========\n  [open] sev=medium fresh=? id=01M5RK2YNSW8\n    title: None\n    where: ?:485\n    body : `partitionLocalTranscriptSessions` records every `localObjectType` error as \"unavailable\", including failures to run git at all (context cancellation, timeout, spawn or lock errors). Because the export is now fatal only when zero sessions are usable, a transient git failure silently drops sessions and republishes a shrunken corpus. Return runner/context errors as errors, and treat only a confirmed\n  [open] sev=medium fresh=? id=01M5RHZZR905\n    title: None\n    where: ?:485\n    body : Any failure of the object-type probe is now treated as 'session unavailable' and skipped. That includes transient git or runner errors, not only a missing object. The old code aborted the export in that case. Now one flaky `cat-file` call can drop sessions, and the export still succeeds as long as one session is usable. That publishes a silently shrunken corpus. Only a definitive 'object missing'","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"050402c4-5948-4de5-a647-9d28125d021d","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:26:08.911Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=========== PR#477 (trail 388) ===========\n  [open] sev=low fresh=? id=01M5QWT2Y3Q1\n    title: None\n    where: ?:205\n    body : `readMCPFrame` allocates `make([]byte, length)` from the child's `Content-Length` with no upper bound. A misbehaving binary can make doctor try a multi-GB allocation before the timeout applies. Cap the length (for example a few MiB) and return an error beyond it.\n  [open] sev=low fresh=? id=01M5QM1M0BN3\n    title: None\n    where: ?:177\n    body : `readMCPFrame` allocates `make([]byte, length)` from the server-supplied `Content-Length` with no upper bound. A wrong or misbehaving binary can announce a huge length and cause a panic or out-of-memory error in doctor. Cap the length, which is the bounded-frames requirement at MCP boundaries.\n  [open] sev=medium fresh=? id=01M5QM1KZVGF\n    title: None\n    where: ?:219\n    body : With the opt-in set, `checkMCPSurfaceReachable` uses `os.Executable()`, which under `go test` is the test binary. The probe runs `<testbinary> mcp`, and the child re-runs the whole suite, including this test. That spawns another child, so the recursion is bounded only by the 20s probe timeouts. Inject the binary path, or stub the probe, in this test.\n=========== PR#483 (trail 394) ===========\n  [open] sev=medium fresh=? id=01M5R8FS7JTP\n    title: None\n    where: ?:1259\n    body : The oversize skip is applied to the identity capture, the full index build and `collectHistorySessionDigests`. The short-term delta path in `history_delta.go` also calls `readHistorySessionInventoryFile`, and `shortTermCanonicalInputRefusal` still treats `memory_input_too_large` as a refusal of the entire delta. A single oversize transcript therefore still blocks the overlay for every other sessio\n=========== PR#484 (trail 395) ===========\n  [open] sev=low fresh=? id=01M5RFGAVDQ2\n    title: None\n    where: ?:323\n    body : `graphContextAllowsAncestor` memoizes the probe result even when the probe failed (timeout, cancelled ctx, transient subprocess error). That permanently caches `false` for the binary for the life of the process, so a provider that supports `--allow-ancestor` is never asked for it again. Cache only successful probe results (a parsed report) and let failures retry.\n  [open] sev=medium fresh=? id=01M5R9TCX0J1\n    title: None\n    where: ?:264\n    body : `Unreliable` is built only from changed files that the answer returned records for. The `graphContextStale` contract says an ancestor store has already dropped the records for changed files, so those paths will mostly be absent from `symbols` and `tests`. `Unreliable` will then usually be empty even when the answer is incomplete, and a reader could take that as 'nothing unreliable'. The paths the \n=========== PR#489 (trail 400) ===========\n  [open] sev=medium fresh=? id=01M5RK2YNSW8\n    title: None\n    where: ?:485\n    body : `partitionLocalTranscriptSessions` records every `localObjectType` error as \"unavailable\", including failures to run git at all (context cancellation, timeout, spawn or lock errors). Because the export is now fatal only when zero sessions are usable, a transient git failure silently drops sessions and republishes a shrunken corpus. Return runner/context errors as errors, and treat only a confirmed\n  [open] sev=medium fresh=? id=01M5RHZZR905\n    title: None\n    where: ?:485\n    body : Any failure of the object-type probe is now treated as 'session unavailable' and skipped. That includes transient git or runner errors, not only a missing object. The old code aborted the export in that case. Now one flaky `cat-file` call can drop sessions, and the export still succeeds as long as one session is usable. That publishes a silently shrunken corpus. Only a definitive 'object missing'","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8b555f99-4719-4b3d-b0f5-fac6423567e7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-firstrun-gate","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-firstrun-gate","branch":"fix/firstrun-agent-hook-paths","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"entireio","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entiredb","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/entire.io","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-firstrun-gate","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d9c89d8a-a612-4bc8-b81e-3008446374b2","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-firstrun-gate","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
