e. Prefer reusing the existing sentinel over a new error. If the delta genuinely cannot be partial for a sound reason, say so with the evidence instead of forcing it.\n\nBefore you start, run an anchored search for BOTH the identifier and the error-code string across internal/ so you do not repeat my miss — report every call site you found and what you did about each.\n\nNON-NEGOTIABLE verification, in this order:\n1. Targeted tests green: `rtk proxy env GOMAXPROCS=1 go test ./internal/cli/ -run '<your pattern>' -count=1 -p 1 -parallel 1`. Confirm with -v that your test NAMES actually ran — a `-run` pattern matching nothing also prints \"ok\".\n2. VERIFIED-BY-WEAKENING: for EACH new/changed guard, patch the production code so it SHOULD fail, run it, confirm RED, restore. Verify your patch applied (unique match) before trusting any green; a weakening that stays green means the test proves nothing.\n3. Full gate: `mise run test:prepush`. Redirect to a file and grep the log for '^FAIL' and the recorded exit — the task is one `set -e` script so only its first line echoes. Never trust a bare exit 0 over an unread log.\n4. The three existing #483 guards MUST still pass: TestHistoryIndexSkipsAnOversizeTranscriptAndIndexesTheRest, TestOversizeTranscriptIsSkippedByEveryInventoryReader, TestStoreSizeRefusalClassifiesAsTheSkippableOversizeError. So must main's TestOverridableProductionBoundsKeepTheirDefaults (it pins that a test's bound override does not leak).\n\nThen `git add` only files you changed, commit (conventional scoped subject; body explains WHY; NO AI/Claude attribution footer of any kind), `git push origin fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize`.\n\nEnv notes: this shell sets FORCE_COLOR=3 and breaks colour-assert tests on correct code — reproduce on main before believing such a failure. Use rtk. Never bare `git stash` (shared across worktrees).\n\nREPORT BACK caveman-ultra compressed, no padding: every call site your search found + disposition; files+lines changed;