{"parentUuid":"afd0ae0e-273d-41b7-8aed-2299421de36e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNLMbT7uXNXwj6s1y8mJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XQeBGwfVTjtMF1PPzvbt5t","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-b2-staleness; git add internal/cli/agent_surface.go internal/cli/graph_context.go internal/cli/graph_context_capability_test.go internal/cli/graph_context_staleness_test.go && git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(brief): remember only a definitive ancestor probe, and carry the excluded count\n\nTwo agent-review findings on this branch, both correct.\n\nThe probe returned a bare bool, so \"ran, feature absent\" and \"did not run\" were\nthe same answer, and the memo cached both. One timed-out probe therefore marked\na provider unsupported for the life of the process, and a provider that does\nsupport ancestor queries was never asked again. It now reports whether the\nanswer is definitive, and only a definitive answer is stored. A binary that\nrejects the `graph` verb is definitive -- it is the wrong kind of binary and\nwill answer identically every time; a timeout or a failure to spawn is not, and\nmalformed JSON could be a truncated read as easily as a binary that cannot\nspeak JSON, so neither is remembered. It still fails closed in every case.\n\nSeparately, Unreliable can only name paths the answer actually returned records\nfor -- and an ancestor store has already dropped the records for changed files,\nwhich are exactly those paths. So Unreliable is empty in the common case even\nwhen the answer is incomplete, and on its own it reads as \"nothing to worry\nabout\". The provider sends excluded_records for precisely this reason and brief\nwas re-emitting four of its five fields, dropping the one that distinguishes an\nincomplete answer from a complete one. It is carried through now.\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1; git push -q origin feat/brief-ancestor-staleness && echo pushed","description":"Commit and push 484's fixes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":646,"cache_read_input_tokens":270705,"output_tokens":657,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":646,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":657,"cache_read_input_tokens":270705,"cache_creation_input_tokens":646,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":646},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01XQeBGwfVTjtMF1PPzvbt5t":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-b2-staleness; git add internal/cli/agent_surface.go internal/cli/graph_context.go internal/cli/graph_context_capability_test.go internal/cli/graph_context_staleness_test.go && git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(brief): remember only a definitive ancestor probe, and carry the excluded count\n\nTwo agent-review findings on this branch, both correct.\n\nThe probe returned a bare bool, so \"ran, feature absent\" and \"did not run\" were\nthe same answer, and the memo cached both. One timed-out probe therefore marked\na provider unsupported for the life of the process, and a provider that does\nsupport ancestor queries was never asked again. It now reports whether the\nanswer is definitive, and only a definitive answer is stored. A binary that\nrejects the `graph` verb is definitive -- it is the wrong kind of binary and\nwill answer identically every time; a timeout or a failure to spawn is not, and\nmalformed JSON could be a truncated read as easily as a binary that cannot\nspeak JSON, so neither is remembered. It still fails closed in