{"parentUuid":"b041d6b0-688f-4f27-80a0-1e1f116f9e72","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNLoM9t2Jd6vVkBKM3EK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Progress while the three agents run:\n\n**Sequential merge simulation, pass 1 — the thing the graph session flagged as missing.** All 13 PRs merge cleanly in order (`473, 476, 482, 478, 474, 480, 479, 481, 488, 489, 477, 483, 484`), and the combined tree compiles with zero `vet` findings. That rules out the cross-PR API-break class — e.g. one PR renaming something another still calls.\n\nIt does **not** yet rule out the break they actually hit on #381: a test asserting a file another PR deliberately stopped writing. That compiles fine and only fails when the suite runs. So this is pass 1 of 2, and I'm not claiming the integration is clean yet.\n\nI've held the suite run rather than start it: load is at 7.0 with three agents' test binaries already going, and running concurrent full suites on this machine is a mistake I've made before. It goes next, and it has to be re-run anyway — three of the thirteen branches will change when the agents push.\n\nTwo notes on how I got here, since both were nearly silent failures:\n\n- The first simulation loop reported `#473 clean` and then stopped. Not a conflict — the shell's working directory was reset out from under the loop, so it never reached branch 2. A loop that stops early after one success looks exactly like a short clean run. Re-ran with `git -C` on every command so nothing depended on cwd.\n- `go vet` then printed `vet-exit=` — empty, because `PIPESTATUS` didn't survive the way I'd written it. An empty exit code is not a zero; I re-ran it capturing the status directly before believing the clean result.\n\nStill outstanding: #489, #483 and #477 with their agents, then the skeptic pass on #489, then the integration suite. Nothing is blocked on anything I can't do, except Approvals."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":720,"cache_read_input_tokens":279335,"output_tokens":600,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":720,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":600,"cache_read_input_tokens":279335,"cache_creation_input_tokens":720,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":720},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"7690fede-1a51-4157-abe4-8f32ffad28f1","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgNLoLo3Tj5YKK89qVuKV","requestRef":"31402130-6c55-4685-a7ea-430864601554","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"7fe2ef01-42a4-4ad9-aa92-e20ca84583f5","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:42:09.857Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
