{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:23:57.307Z","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>bfcrw94fg</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Aw6eAgQhYLRYefKgbv1PZF</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85/tasks/bfcrw94fg.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Background command \"Run internal/cli suite with 45m cap\" completed (exit code 0)</summary>\n</task-notification>"}
{"parentUuid":"03144769-8006-4ee9-9d55-f7d09d0ad294","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNPxm2B3C8B5uBxGfgYM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**#477 and #483 are both done and verified.** #489 is the last one running.\n\nOn #477 the agent did good work — it proved `:177` and `:205` are one site by tracing the line number across commits, reused the existing 4 MiB `maxMCPFrameBytes` so no bounds-pin test needed touching, and gave a sound reason for *not* reusing `SafeReadAll`: a frame body is an exact-length `ReadFull`, so `LimitReader`+`ReadAll` would consume past the frame boundary and break the following read. It also found that a *negative* Content-Length was being misreported as \"no Content-Length header\" — blaming the server for omitting a header it had sent, in the one check whose whole job is naming causes.\n\nBut I ran a weakening it hadn't, and it mattered: **moving the allocation above the cap check left every test green.** The announced lengths were 4 MiB + 1 and 16 MiB, both harmless to allocate, so the tests proved the error was returned — not that the allocation was avoided, which is the entire point of the finding. The test named `...InsteadOfAllocatingIt` proved nothing about not allocating. Added `math.MaxInt`, which can't be allocated on any platform; the reordering now panics and goes red.\n\nThat's the **third instance of one class in this session**: a test asserting a proxy for the property its name claims. #483's classifier boolean standing in for the publish behaviour, my own #484 construction-layer check standing in for the emitted JSON, and now an error-returned check standing in for an allocation-avoided claim. All three were green suites.\n\nI also checked two claims in #477's report that looked off. One was my error: `make([]byte` appears three times in the file, but two are in comments the agent wrote — its \"exactly one\" was right about code. The other is real but minor: \"17 ok + 3 no-test-files = all 21 packages, all green\" is 20, and the 21st is `internal/cli`, which timed out in that log and was green only in a separate `-timeout 25m` run.\n\nThat timeout is worth flagging beyond this PR, because both agents hit it independently: `internal/cli` takes **232s idle and 805–855s under contention**, against `go test`'s **10m default** that the gate never raises. CI uses `-timeout 30m`, so the local gate cannot pass on this machine while other suites run, and the panic names whichever test was running at the alarm — it reads exactly like a flake in the file you just touched. Recorded."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":557,"cache_read_input_tokens":339759,"output_tokens":806,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":557,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":806,"cache_read_input_tokens":339759,"cache_creation_input_tokens":557,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":557},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f3f71f25-a439-4240-8d72-2f51e0bdc1cd","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgNPxkfqKeNrj4baDWXnL","requestRef":"23f488e3-d089-4f20-a7b9-31655840b396","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"3c890af0-7f8d-4824-a81d-54fa6ab218c8","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:23:40.654Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-mcp-reach","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version"