ll, non-blob.\n  - TestCancelledContextFailsTheExportRatherThanShrinkingIt — asserts errors.Is(err, context.Canceled).\n  - TestUnavailableDiagnosticsKeepTheirErrorIdentity — identity through both the partition and the strict wrapper.\n  New fixtures probedFixture/probeRunner/stubExitError: the old vanishedFixture never reaches the git probe at all (its vanished session is absent from the snapshot, classified from data), so no pre-existing test covered this code path.\n  \n  GATE\n  - Targeted: `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test ./internal/cli/ -run '<13 patterns>' -count=1 -p 1 -parallel 1` -> ok 16.7s.\n  - `mise run test:prepush` -> **exit 0**, **^FAIL count 0**, log read in full (1186B/19 lines, all 15 testable packages ok, internal/cli 322s; gofmt and vet silent, and set -e means they passed). Independently: rest-of-suite exit 0, `gofmt -l -s .` empty, `go vet ./...` exit 0, `go test ./internal/cli -timeout 45m` exit 0 / 0 FAIL / 396s.\n  - The 4 required existing tests pass, incl. TestFilelessMigrationPreservesUnrecoverableExcludedCache (both subtests) and TestFilelessMigrationRecoversExcludedSessionAfterInclude.\n  \n  PRE-EXISTING LANDMINE WORTH KNOWING (not caused by me)\n  My first `mise run test:prepush` FAILED: `panic: test timed out after 10m0s`, internal/cli at 600.5s, with 20 unrelated tests all 0-9s in flight — go test's DEFAULT 10m cap, not a hang. test:prepush passes no -timeout while CI uses `go test -timeout 20m` (.github/workflows/{nightly,release}.yml:92/152). Under load this gate fails on correct code. Also: my first two attempts produced a 410-byte truncated log because the redirect fd was shared with a still-running child — a bare exit code there was a lie. Reliable recipe: `{ cmd > log 2>&1; echo $? > log.exit; }` backgrounded, then block on a mkfifo signal.\n  \n  COULD NOT VERIFY\n  - Windows: batching is gated off there, so every probe takes the per-exec path. Logic is platform-independent and exit 1 is git's documented status, but untested on Windows (CI will cover it).\n  - Behaviour against a real promisor partial clone (I proved the equivalent by deleting the loose object, which produces the same `could not get object info` / exit-1 pair).\n  - Exit codes measured on git 2.54.0 only.\n  - I did not run the export end-to-end against a real brain; all evidence is unit-level.\n  Recorded two durable facts: fact:87b93d2c5a0fe22d9d4aba6f (architecture.export.gotcha, the cat-file exit codes) and fact:a0fb500464bea7c006e5b1aa (constraints.invariants.general, classify on the answer + collect []error not []string).","handback":true,"handbackReportText":"FINDING 01M5RK2YNSW8 = CORRECT. FIXED. Commit ce56353577d2838aaee4656616dba1bc6bce2aa6, pushed db2d4ff9..ce563535 on fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints. No rebase, no merge, base db2d4ff9 intact. Worktree clean. No AI footer (Entire-Checkpoint trailer is the capture hook's).\n\nFILES (5, all /Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished/internal/cli/)\n- git_catfile_batch.go +73/-4: sentinel errCatFileBatchMissing RENAMED errGitObjectMissing (:45-52, no longer batch-only); new gitObjectAbsentExitCode=1 (:54-59); new `type exitCoder interface{ ExitCode() int }` (:61-65); localObjectType :348-378 now wraps per-exec misses; new localObjectMissingConfirmed :380-408.\n- transcript_store.go +57/-7: validateLocalTranscriptSessions :414-430 returns unavailable[0] AS-IS; partitionLocalTranscriptSessions signature ([]exportSession, **[]error**, error) :453-534; chunk-probe `if err != nil || kind != \"blob\"` replaced by a 3-way switch :490-513.\n- export.go +7/-2: caller :360-366 returns unavailable[0] directly, warning uses %v.\n- export_vanished_checkpoint_test.go +193, git_catfile_batch_test.go +49: 4 new tests + fixtures.\n\nHOW \"MISSING\" IS CLASSIFIED (no stderr text matching anywhere)\n- Batch path: already had git's machine-readable `<spec> missing` record -> errGitObjectMissing. Pre-existing; now the general sentinel.\n- Per-exec path: `cat-file -t` gives NO machine-readable miss. MEASURED git 2.54.0: exit 128 + `fatal:` for missing path / missing ref / pruned blob — and 128 is identical for \"not a git repository\" and a bad config value. So on failure it asks a second, narrower question and reads the EXIT CODE: `git cat-file -e <spec>` exits **1, silent, no stderr** for an object that resolved but is not present, **0** when present (=> the -t failure was transient => stays an error), 128 otherwise (=> stays an error). Precedent in-repo: git_harden_filters.go:131-132 classifies `git config`'s exit 1 the same way. Extra spawn only on an already-failed probe.\n- ctx.Err() != nil short-circuits before the confirming probe.\n- exitCoder interface rather than *exec.ExitError: *exec.ExitError satisfies it, matches the recorded convention (capabilities as interfaces), and lets a fake runner model exit 1.\n- DELIBERATE ASYMMETRY, disclosed: per-exec is STRICTER than batch — an unresolvable spec (128) refuses the export where the batch child would partition. Fail-safe: can only over-refuse, never silently shrink. Documented at git_catfile_batch.go:400-406.\n- kind != \"blob\" with err==nil is now an ERROR, not unavailable (snapshot fault, uniform; restores pre-#489 behaviour for that case).\n\nCOORDINATOR ADDITION — DONE, []string was the right thing to change\nunavailable is now []error, every entry wrapping its cause with %w; strict wrapper returns unavailable[0] instead of errors.New(string); export.go returns it as-is. So errors.Is reaches errGitObjectMissing through the wrapper and context.Canceled through the hard-error path. My runner/context error path already used %w before your message; the []string flattening did not.\n\nWEAKENINGS — 9, each confirmed RED then restored (sha-verified identical after each)\n1. `case errors.Is(err,errGitObjectMissing)` -> `case err != nil` (restores the bug): RED x6 (5 subtests + cancellation).\n2. delete non-blob guard: RED snapshot_path_is_not_a_blob.\n3. drop ctx.Err() guard in classifier: RED cancellation (classified missing via the scripted exit 1 — exactly the trap).\n4. confirming probe accepts any failure: RED x4 + RED real-git test.\n5. present object reads as missing: RED object_is_present_after_all.\n6. per-exec never types a miss: RED x2 incl. real-git.\n7. gitObjectAbsentExitCode 1 -> 2: RED x2 incl. real-git.\n8. runner/context error %w -> %v: RED TestCancelledContextFailsTheExportRatherThanShrinkingIt.\n9. unavailable diagnostic %w -> %v, and separately wrapper -> errors.New(...Error()): RED TestUnavailableDiagnosticsKeepTheirErrorIdentity (both).\nEach patch asserted unique-match before trusting any result (one attempt broke the build from a misplaced marker and was redone).\n\nTESTS ADDED\n- TestLocalObjectTypePerExecClassifiesMissingByExitCode — REAL git via perExecOnlyRunner: prunes the loose object, asserts errGitObjectMissing; asserts an unresolvable spec is NOT typed missing. Exit codes proved against git, not against a fixture's belief.\n- TestConfirmedMissingObjectCostsOnlyItsOwnSession\n- TestProbeFailureThatIsNotAMissingObjectFailsTheExport — 6 cases: spawn failure, runner cannot enforce no_egress, child killed (-1), generic 128, object present after all, non-blob.\n- TestCancelledContextFailsTheExportRatherThanShrinkingIt — asserts errors.Is(err, context.Canceled).\n- TestUnavailableDiagnosticsKeepTheirErrorIdentity — identity through both the partition and the strict wrapper.\nNew fixtures probedFixture/probeRunner/stubExitError: the old vanishedFixture never reaches the git probe at all (its vanished session is absent from the snapshot, classified from data), so no pre-existing test covered this code path.\n\nGATE\n- Targeted: `GOMAXPROCS=1 go test ./internal/cli/ -run '<13 patterns>' -count=1 -p 1 -parallel 1` -> ok 16.7s.\n- `mise run test:prepush` -> **exit 0**, **^FAIL count 0**, log read in full (1186B/19 lines, all 15 testable packages ok, internal/cli 322s; gofmt and vet silent, and set -e means they passed). Independently: rest-of-suite exit 0, `gofmt -l -s .` empty, `go vet ./...` exit 0, `go test ./internal/cli -timeout 45m` exit 0 / 0 FAIL / 396s.\n- The 4 required existing tests pass, incl. TestFilelessMigrationPreservesUnrecoverableExcludedCache (both subtests) and TestFilelessMigrationRecoversExcludedSessionAfterInclude.\n\nPRE-EXISTING LANDMINE WORTH KNOWING (not caused by me)\nMy first `mise run test:prepush` FAILED: `panic: test timed out after 10m0s`, internal/cli at 600.5s, with 20 unrelated tests all 0-9s in flight — go test's DEFAULT 10m cap, not a hang. test:prepush passes no -timeout while CI uses `go test -timeout 20m` (.github/workflows/{nightly,release}.yml:92/152). Under load this gate fails on correct code. Also: my first two attempts produced a 410-byte truncated log because the redirect fd was shared with a still-running child — a bare exit code there was a lie. Reliable recipe: `{ cmd > log 2>&1; echo $? > log.exit; }` backgrounded, then block on a mkfifo signal.\n\nCOULD NOT VERIFY\n- Windows: batching is gated off there, so every probe takes the per-exec path. Logic is platform-independent and exit 1 is git's documented status, but untested on Windows (CI will cover it).\n- Behaviour against a real promisor partial clone (I proved the equivalent by deleting the loose object, which produces the same `could not get object info` / exit-1 pair).\n- Exit codes measured on git 2.54.0 only.\n- I did not run the export end-to-end against a real brain; all evidence is unit-level.\nRecorded two durable facts: fact:87b93d2c5a0fe22d9d4aba6f (architecture.export.gotcha, the cat-file exit codes) and fact:a0fb500464bea7c006e5b1aa (constraints.invariants.general, classify on the answer + collect []error not []string)."},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-mcp-reach","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
