{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","id":"31d9dd26-0926-4941-83b6-2268a1e40359","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:33:40.118Z","version":"2.1.310","querySource":"repl_main_thread","shapeHash":"24017389debf7cd8bde5028ecf29c4ee6405c6fe767d12c483cd96a0e96b3788","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","context-1m-2025-08-07","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":64000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"xhigh"}},"base":"a8460aa6-cd9b-4baa-9f81-63747b20e39c","keep":549,"tail":["2c2b12edc69b6c032195a7d8bab62aa26963264f36f71085641a5c5f550ee26e","5e26820bbb8666ec0542d48c7d5545bf1132a60395c97990dd657f3d0fd40d4d","3021337c8bb4e053f892c4f29a67b938bcd49ce00e0e14d1e3a3eec26a1a99f5"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",551,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"de16d8001466ab81d7cea4fdafa4fc16f89fd6fc70f02169946792381ec4f7d2"}
{"parentUuid":"44e84b90-2da6-4add-b2ac-1495096c85f9","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14364695 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a17e3095-a1ee-4156-a00f-fd27e927be69","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:33:40.087Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14364695 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"a17e3095-a1ee-4156-a00f-fd27e927be69","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNQjt8YupbDypczqLZ6t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UzmTpXofuP4rrHqVreWeLY","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"merge-graph-fixes-and-improve-agent-adoption","summary":"All four findings landed; one design call found","message":"All four findings are fixed, pushed and green — plus the skeptic pass you asked for on #489, which found one thing you should carry into the handoff as a DESIGN CALL, not a defect.\n\nFINAL STATE, all green, all conflict-free, Approvals the only blocker:\n  #477 feat/mcp-surface-reachable           17f6bdc3\n  #483 fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize  201fe6eb\n  #484 feat/brief-ancestor-staleness         8d3f4ce8\n  #489 fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints ce563535\n\n#489 SKEPTIC PASS. The fix classifies \"object missing\" by `cat-file -e` EXIT CODE rather than stderr prose. I reproduced the codes on real git 2.54.0 myself rather than trusting the report: present=0 silent, resolved-but-absent=1 silent, unresolvable=128 with fatal:. Sound, and 9 weakenings were red. It also adopted the error-identity point I sent — `unavailable` is now []error wrapping with %w, so errors.Is reaches both errGitObjectMissing and context.Canceled.\n\nTHE DESIGN CALL. I then tested the one case the agent disclosed it could not: a promisor partial clone. The probe runs through runCheckpointGitLocal, which sets GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1. Measured: a blob that is absent locally but FETCHABLE from the promisor remote also exits 1 silent — byte-identical to a pruned object that is gone for good. (With lazy fetch allowed it exits 0, because it fetches.) So under no-egress on a partial clone, \"absent\" is genuinely ambiguous and the code cannot tell the two apart without egress. #489 resolves it toward \"gone\" and skips the session, and `unavailableSessionsAreFatal` refuses only when usable==0 — there is no PARTIAL-shrink guard. A previously larger published corpus can therefore be replaced by a smaller one with only a warning.\n\nThat configuration is live, not hypothetical: cli's brain was frozen earlier in this session precisely because transcript and metadata blobs were promisor-absent, and I fixed it by fetching 422 of them by hand. It is also the same promisor shape as your #372.\n\nI deliberately did NOT patch it, because both obvious fixes are wrong:\n  - \"a promisor remote means absent might be fetchable, so refuse\" re-breaks #489 exactly where it was needed — cli IS a promisor clone and its squash-destroyed commits are unfetchable anywhere.\n  - \"refuse if the new corpus is smaller\" breaks `privacy exclude`, which legitimately shrinks via tombstones — which is what #488 does.\nA correct guard has to be tombstone-aware, so it is a design decision and it is on Suhaan's list, recorded in brain at architecture.export.constraint. #489 is still a strict improvement on what it replaced (which refused everything, permanently, and preserved nothing), so I would not hold it for this.\n\nALSO WORTH YOUR D2: both agents independently hit a pre-existing landmine. `internal/cli` runs 232s idle but 805-855s under contention, against go test's 10m DEFAULT, which test:prepush never raises (CI uses -timeout 20m in nightly/release). Under parallel load the gate fails on correct code and the panic names whichever test was running at the alarm. If your fresh-env runs touch this package, use GOFLAGS=-timeout=30m rather than trusting a red.\n\nBrain is FINAL as of now. Go ahead with D2. Sequential-merge sim pass 1 is done on my side: all 13 merge clean in order and the combined tree compiles with 0 vet findings; the suite run on the combined tree is the remaining half and I am running it now that the agents have freed the CPU.","type":"message","recipient":"merge-graph-fixes-and-improve-agent-adoption","recipient_kind":"name","content":"All four findings are fixed, pushed and green — p…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3221,"cache_read_input_tokens":356819,"output_tokens":1414,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3221,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1414,"cache_read_input_tokens":356819,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3221,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3221},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01UzmTpXofuP4rrHqVreWeLY":{"to":"merge-graph-fixes-and-improve-agent-adoption","summary":"All four findings landed; one design call found","message":"All four findings are fixed, pushed and green — plus the skeptic pass you asked for on #489, which found one thing you should carry into the handoff as a DESIGN CALL, not a defect.\n\nFINAL STATE, all green, all conflict-free, Approvals the only blocker:\n  #477 feat/mcp-surface-reachable           17f6bdc3\n  #483 fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize  201fe6eb\n  #484 feat/brief-ancestor-staleness         8d3f4ce8\n  #489 fix/export-skips-vanished-checkpoints ce563535\n\n#489 SKEPTIC PASS. The fix classifies \"object missing\" by `cat-file -e` EXIT CODE rather than stderr prose. I reproduced the codes on real git 2.54.0 myself rather than trusting the report: present=0 silent, resolved-but-absent=1 silent, unresolvable=128 with fatal:. Sound, and 9 weakenings were red. It also adopted the error-identity point I sent — `unavailable` is now []error wrapping with %w, so errors.Is reaches both errGitObjectMissing and context.Canceled.\n\nTHE DESIGN CALL. I then tested the one case the agent disclosed it could not: a promisor partial clone. The probe runs through runCheckpointGitLocal, which sets GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1. Measured: a blob that is absent locally but FETCHABLE from the promisor remote also exits 1 silent — byte-identical to a pruned object that is gone for good. (With lazy fetch allowed it exits 0, because it fetches.) So under no-egress on a partial clone, \"absent\" is genuinely ambiguous and the code cannot tell the two apart without egress. #489 resolves it toward \"gone\" and skips the session, and `unavailableSessionsAreFatal` refuses only when usable==0 — there is no PARTIAL-shrink guard. A previously larger published corpus can therefore be replaced by a smaller one with only a warning.\n\nThat configuration is live, not hypothetical: cli's brain was frozen earlier in this session precisely because transcript and metadata blobs were promisor-absent, and I fixed it by fetching 422 of them by hand. It is also the same promisor shape as your #372.\n\nI deliberately did NOT patch it, because both obvious fixes are wrong:\n  - \"a promisor remote means absent might be fetchable, so refuse\" re-breaks #489 exactly where it was needed — cli IS a promisor clone and its squash-destroyed commits are unfetchable anywhere.\n  - \"refuse if the new corpus is smaller\" breaks `privacy exclude`, which legitimately shrinks via tombstones — which is what #488 does.\nA correct guard has to be tombstone-aware, so it is a design decision and it is on Suhaan's list, recorded in brain at architecture.export.constraint. #489 is still a strict improvement on what it replaced (which refused everything, permanently, and preserved nothing), so I would not hold it for this.\n\nALSO WORTH YOUR D2: both agents independently hit a pre-existing landmine. `internal/cli` runs 232s idle but 805-855s under contention, against go test's 10m DEFAULT, which test:prepush never raises (CI uses -timeout 20m in nightly/release). Under parallel load the gate fails on correct code and the panic names whichever test was running at the alarm. If your fresh-env runs touch this package, use GOFLAGS=-timeout=30m rather than trusting a red.\n\nBrain is FINAL as of now. Go ahead with D2. Sequential-merge sim pass 1 is done on my side: all 13 merge clean in order and the combined tree compiles with 0 vet findings; the suite run on the combined tree is the remaining half and I am running it now that the agents have freed the CPU."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"2007e7dc-9982-4fd0-bd50-13983b87eb73","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgNQjsoTP8BmQz3Ae3bb4","requestRef":"31d9dd26-0926-4941-83b6-2268a1e40359","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"c539bc7e-c20f-4ec6-9b10-6235cfcf9a39","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:34:00.319Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-vanished","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
