{"parentUuid":"96250b88-f5e4-4bbd-923c-2935193b1675","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14321129 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5f23a234-ea88-4b44-a5aa-b52fc28e04c7","timestamp":"2026-10-25T05:45:09.130Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14321129 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"80327498-7bd2-42a4-985a-9acba8ccaf85","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/brain-history-oversize","sessionId":"93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"floofy-discovering-bachman"}
{"parentUuid":"5f23a234-ea88-4b44-a5aa-b52fc28e04c7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgNRcgRXW6nmj2FvQMyQj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015WMUhxW8eYWyMZiJL1jFfm","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/93ae8948-c612-4072-8e70-2750e80df9ce/scratchpad; cat > \"$S/b9.json\" <<'JSON'\n[{\"id\":\"export-family-sequential-merge\",\"lane\":\"brain\",\"owner\":\"claude\",\"status\":\"done\",\n  \"title\":\"INTEGRATION PASS: draft PR #493 (DO NOT MERGE) has all 13 combined in merge order @9751b7d4. Combined tree: go test exit 0, 19 ok + 3 no-test = 22/22, 0 FAIL, gofmt+vet clean. Pushed for the -race/Windows coverage no local run could reach. 3 resolution patches saved\"},\n {\"id\":\"upstream-drift-invalidates-sim\",\"lane\":\"brain\",\"owner\":\"claude\",\"status\":\"done\",\n  \"title\":\"LESSON: pairwise-clean has a shelf life. main gained #490+#491 MID-SESSION and #473 - clean 2h earlier - began conflicting in workspace.go. Re-run the merge sim immediately before the real merges, not once\"}]\nJSON\npython3 \"$S/board_update.py\" \"$S/b9.json\"; M=/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory; cat > \"$M/pairwise-clean-has-a-shelf-life.md\" <<'EOF'\n---\nname: pairwise-clean-has-a-shelf-life\ndescription: \"A merge-conflict check expires: main moves under you, so re-run the sequential sim immediately before the real merges\"\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nVerifying thirteen branches merge cleanly against `main` is worth doing and is **not** durable.\nTwo hours after a clean full-order simulation, `#473` conflicted in `internal/cli/workspace.go` —\nnot because the branch changed, but because `main` gained two PRs (`#490` workspace extraction,\n`#491`) while the work was in flight.\n\nTwo distinct hazards, and only the first is the one people warn about:\n- **cross-PR:** merging one PR changes `main` for the next. A semantic break needs no textual\n  conflict — a peer's integration branch caught a test asserting a file another PR had\n  deliberately stopped writing. No per-PR gate can see it.\n- **upstream drift:** someone else merges while you verify. Nothing in your set changed and the\n  answer still went stale.\n\n**How to apply:** treat the sequential merge simulation as a step performed *immediately before*\nthe real merges, never as a result you quote from earlier. `git -C <scratch> fetch` first, and\nre-check. Build the combined tree in a scratch worktree, run the whole suite on it (not just a\ncompile — `go vet` passes through the semantic break), and push it as a draft DO-NOT-MERGE PR so\nCI covers `-race` and Windows, which a local run cannot. Save each resolution as\n`git diff <merge>^2 <merge> -- <conflicted files>` — against parent 2, so the patch is the\nbranch's contribution and not the megabyte of everything `main` dragged in.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\np=\"/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\nline=\"- [Pairwise-clean has a shelf life](pairwise-clean-has-a-shelf-life.md) — main moved mid-session and a clean branch began conflicting; re-sim right before merging\\n\"\nif \"pairwise-clean-has-a-shelf-life\" not in s:\n    s = s.rstrip(\"\\n\")+\"\\n\"+line\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"MEMORY.md bytes:\", len(s.encode()))\nPY","description":"Close the board row and record the lesson"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1739,"cache_read_input_tokens":401947,"output_tokens":1347,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1739,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1347,"cache_read_input_token