kpoint repository names its promisor remote by URL (remote.https://github.com/entireio/cli-checkpoints.git.promisor) and does NOT set extensions.partialclone, so a detector written against remote.origin.promisor or against that extension would pass every fake-runner test and miss the only repository the guard exists for. I verified both facts on cli's real config.\n\nFour weakenings, each a real `--- FAIL` and not a build failure:\n  - drop the promisor condition  -> RED on the partial-clone test\n  - detector always true         -> RED on the full-clone test AND on the agent's #489 test\n                                    (so the guard is provably narrow)\n  - pattern narrowed to origin   -> RED on the real-git url-named subtest, while the\n                                    fake-runner tests stay GREEN. That is the point: the\n                                    fakes could not have caught it.\n\nTwo consequences for your page:\n1. #489's head changes once the gate passes. I will send the SHA.\n2. #493 then holds a stale #489. I will re-push the integration branch and re-run its suite.\n3. DECISIONS-FOR-YOU.md §7 stops being a decision. I will rewrite it as \"closed, here is what\n   it was\", so the combined table should drop that row rather than carry it to Suhaan.\n\nNothing in your lane is affected."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
