in's own TestOverridableProductionBoundsKeepTheirDefaults.\n\nNote `go build ./...` does NOT compile test files — that exact trap already hid breakage on this branch once. Use `go vet ./internal/cli/` and expect to follow renames into `*_test.go`. Check for an existing import alias before inventing one.\n\nVERIFY, in order:\n1. `go vet ./internal/cli/` exits 0. Capture its status directly — `go vet ... | head` reports head's status, not vet's.\n2. Run the tests above with -v and confirm the NAMES appear; a `-run` matching nothing also prints \"ok\".\n3. PROVE THE RESOLUTION KEPT THE FEATURE: delete the sentinel skip in the identity reader, confirm `--- FAIL: TestHistoryIndexSkipsAnOversizeTranscriptAndIndexesTheRest` (and likely TestOversizeTranscriptIsSkippedByEveryInventoryReader), restore. A `[build failed]` is NOT a red; keep the package compiling and verify your patch applied as a unique match — on this file a naive patch has matched TWO sites before, and the green run that followed proved nothing.\n4. Full gate: `GOFLAGS=-timeout=40m mise run test:prepush > /tmp/g483.log 2>&1; echo \"EXIT=$?\" >> /tmp/g483.log`. The `-timeout` is REQUIRED: internal/cli is 232s idle but 805-855s under parallel load against go test's 10m default, and other agents are running suites right now. Grep for `--- FAIL` and the recorded EXIT; never trust a bare exit code over an unread log.\n\nThen commit (conventional subject; body states what main extracted, what you kept, the weakening; NO AI/Claude attribution footer) and `git push origin fix/history-index-tolerates-oversize`.\n\nEnv: FORCE_COLOR=3 is set here and fails colour-assert tests on correct code — reproduce on main before believing one. Never bare `git stash` (shared across worktrees).\n\nREPORT caveman-ultra compressed: conflicted hunks + resolution; renames followed in tests; the weakening and its exact `--- FAIL` line; gate EXIT + FAIL count + package count; commit SHA; anything unverified.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/c